nprolog_slice2_socket_bridge('2026-11-25, operator direction: multi-transport support ("why just REPL?"); slice 2 implemented on the same branch/PR: shipped prolog/star-logic-bridge.pl (protocol star-logic-nprolog-bridge-1: hello handshake, ping liveness, quit unblock), launched with -r -c ./star-logic-bridge.pl and adapter-pinned bridge directory (./ consult names resolve against child CWD ahead of NPROLOG_HOME per builtin.c prolog_file_name). Bridge is the single trusted package identity (sha256-pinned, revalidated pre-launch; package expectations must match it or fail closed). Wire verified from upstream C source (superset.c npl 5.20): send_socket writes exactly 256 bytes = payload + strcpy NUL + uninitialized stack padding (payloads bounded 255, receivers truncate at first NUL; disclosure is an upstream-contribution candidate), recv_socket is one raw read so coalesced frames lose data => strict lock-step, create_server_socket binds INADDR_ANY and blocks in accept and never reports the port => adapter probes a free loopback port and retries once on probe-to-bind race. 19 pure + 6 integration tests green vs pinned engine; descriptor capabilities still empty (query operations ride this bridge in later slices). Transport roadmap: batch -s next (slice 3), then compile_file/1 accelerator with query ops; -n experimental').
nprolog_slice3_batch_validation('2026-11-25: nprolog-batch-validate implemented (slice 3, same branch/PR). Live verification overturned the -s doc shape: -s FILE consults then exits EXIT_SUCCESS unconditionally - consult failures, syntax errors, and missing files all exit 0, and a clean consult prints nothing (not even the banner; -s exits before printing it). Exit codes cannot validate a load; the contract is fail-closed on output: valid iff exit 0 AND empty stdout after ANSI strip; any diagnostic, nonzero exit, timeout, or output over the capture bound is invalid with a bounded ANSI-stripped diagnostic; report carries sha256 of the exact validated bytes; dotless names refused before launch because upstream consult appends .pl to dot-free names (silently targeting a different file). Consumption: a CI/pre-consult gate answering "does this rule pack load under npl". 28 tests green (21 pure + 7 integration); nix flake check -L green; branch logic/n-prolog-backend at e6ffe8ef on forgejo PR nsaspy/star-lang#218').
